<title>HONG KONG: Benefit Bright sets loan for Hong Kong project.</title>
<headline>Benefit Bright sets loan for Hong Kong project.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following loan issue is in general syndication, bankers said.</p>
<p>The borrower is Benefit Bright Ltd, a vehicle of a consortium comprising Sino Land Co Ltd, Kerry Properties, China Overseas Land and Investment and the Bank of China Group.</p>
<p>Proceeds are to be used to finance a property development in Hong Kong. The project, the Tai Kok Tsui Mass Transit Railway Package Two, is one of many projects associated with Hong Kong's new airport.</p>
<p>Details are as follows:</p>
<p>BORROWER  BENEFIT BRIGHT</p>
<p>  AMOUNT    HK$8 BLN     TYPE     TERM LOAN</p>
<p>  MARGIN    HIBOR+140    MATURITY 4 YRS    AVGE LIFE --</p>
<p>  PUTS	NONE	   CALLS    NONE     LAUNCHED  --</p>
<p>  REPAYMENT BULLET	 HOME     HONG KONG</p>
<p>  LEAD	CHINA DEVELOPMENT FINANCE CO, HSBC INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p>ARRANGERS ASIA, DEUTSCHE BANK, HANG SENG BANK, SOCIETE</p>
<p>		GENERALE ASIA, BA ASIA, WESTLB.</p>
<p>ARRANGERS SANWA BANK, TAI FUNG BANK, BOT-MITSUBISHI BHF, FUJI</p>
<p>		BANK, SUMITOMO BANK, CREDITANSTALDT, DAI-ICHI</p>
<p>		KANGYO BANK.</p>
<p>MGT LEVELS AND FEES</p>
<p>		CO-ARGRS AND EXPANDED LEADS HK$160-200 MLN 57.5 BP</p>
<p>		CO-LEAD MANAGERS		HK$110-150 MLN 50   BP</p>
<p>SENIOR MANAGERS HK$ 80-100 MLN 45 BP</p>
<p>		MANAGERS			  HK$ 50- 75 MLN 40   BP</p>
<p>  NOTES    THE ALL-IN RETURN TO SUB-UNDERWRITERS IS 160 BP.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2845-4039</p>
</text>
